<header><p class="st-kicker">principality · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Principality of Castiglione</h1><p class="st-meta">1579 CE – 1773 CE (approx.) · capital Castiglione delle Stiviere</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Lombard state of a Gonzaga branch, birthplace of Saint Aloysius Gonzaga, who gave up its succession to become a Jesuit.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/castiglione-delle-stiviere">Castiglione delle Stiviere</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-garda">Lake Garda</a>, belonged to a cadet branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-gonzaga">Gonzaga</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-mantua">Mantua</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrante-gonzaga-marquis-of-castiglione">Ferrante Gonzaga</a>, its lord, was made marquis by the emperor in 1579, and the state became a principality under his son Francesco in 1612.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The rulers governed a few small towns and farmland as an imperial fief. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferrante-gonzaga-marquis-of-castiglione">Ferrante</a>'s eldest son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aloysius-gonzaga">Aloysius</a>, born in 1568, renounced his rights to join the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> and died in 1591 nursing plague victims in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>; he was canonised in 1726 and the town became a pilgrimage centre. His brother Rodolfo was murdered in 1593 by his own subjects. Later princes faced revolts and imperial intervention.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Prince Ferdinando II was deposed after local unrest, and Austrian troops occupied the state in 1691. After long disputes over compensation for the family, the principality was finally incorporated into Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> in 1773.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/principality-of-castiglione.jpg" alt="Principality of Castiglione" width="320" height="240"><figcaption>Image: Wikimedia Commons · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maremma_Coast-Toskana-Italy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1579 CE – 1773 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>principality</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Castiglione delle Stiviere</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ferrante Gonzaga of Castiglione, Rodolfo Gonzaga, Francesco Gonzaga of Castiglione</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lombard, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Marquisate of Castiglione, Castiglione delle Stiviere</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1676&amp;focus=principality-of-castiglione" aria-label="Principality of Castiglione on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4943 658 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Principality of Castiglione lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5263 914L5229 694M5263 914L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5263 914h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5263 914h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1676&amp;focus=principality-of-castiglione">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
